{
  "id": 531294463,
  "iid": 26480,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "USB HID: Control message dissect/decode improvements",
  "description": "Improve the dissection and decoding of USB HID control messages:\n\n- Add a custom format function to decode the raw value of the `SET_IDLE` Duration field to a human-understandable representation.\n- Add a new Protocol field for the `SET_PROTOCOL` message, including value names for decoding. To be consistent with the standard control message structure and all other control messages, place it as a child beneath wValue.\n- In addition to the setup stage, also dissect the data stage of control messages (where applicable).\n\n<hr>\n\nNotes:\n1. I split this across 3 commits since it felt sensible to me. Let me know if I should squash them.\n2. Is the forward-declaration of `dissect_usb_hid_data` okay? Alternatively I could move the whole function up.\n3. I am aware that the update of `offset` just before a return or function end does nothing. It causes no warning so I left it as-is for correctness, and count on the compiler to optimize it away.",
  "state": "merged",
