      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3826367023,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I forgot that the thousand-separator format-flag is not C standard but POSIX, which is why the Windows build failed:\n\n```\nC:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\epan\\dissectors\\packet-usb-hid.c(5522,42): warning C4476: 'snprintf' : unknown type field character ''' in format specifier [C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\build\\epan\\dissectors\\dissectors.vcxproj]\n         snprintf(buf, ITEM_LABEL_LENGTH, \"%'u ms\", ms);\n                                          ^\n```\n\nSince the values can only go up to 1020, the thousand-separator is not critical; I will just drop the flag and format as a normal integer.",
          "author": {
            "id": 30759163,
            "username": "corubba",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "corubba",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/76e6213842d9e9be8e80ac40cd11cf1747db7c748db2e382c8177e6d7e9beb98?s=80&d=identicon",
